---
// Two-column intro under the hero. Client's own copy: first supplied 28 Sept
// 2026 to replace the lorem ipsum this slot carried from the Elementor
// prototype, then revised by them on 29 Sept 2026.
//
// Rendered on the homepage and on /about/. One source, so the two pages
// cannot drift - a copy change here lands on both.
//
// Layout C from the intro exploration: the same two columns with a hairline
// rule between them, which makes the pairing read as deliberate rather than
// as two paragraphs that happen to sit side by side.
//
// Both columns are paragraphs. The left was an <h2>, which suited the short
// placeholder but not a 173-character sentence - a heading that long is wrong
// for screen readers and search alike. The page still has its headings further
// down ("Our Services", "Industries & Applications", and so on).
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="container grid">
    <p class="lead">
      As a drone survey specialist, Pixel Surveys provides accurate,
      innovative and practical data solutions for a wide range of projects
      across South Australia.
    </p>
    <p class="support">
      Capabilities include drone capture, GNSS processing, surveying and
      geospatial analysis. Each project is tailored to the site, required
      accuracy and deliverables, with the survey method selected to suit the
      project requirements.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: 56px 80px;
    /* See PageHeader: /about/ paints <main> navy, so this declares its own
       white instead of inheriting the body's. */
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
    /* stretch, not start: the support column carries the dividing rule on its
       left edge, so it has to span the full height of the taller column for
       the rule to run the whole way down. */
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  /* Large enough to lead the page without being heading-sized: the old 36px
     was set for a short placeholder line, and this sentence at that size would
     dominate everything below it. */
  .lead {
    font-size: 23px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* The placeholder here was underlined, which was fine on a two-word label
     and would read as a broken link on a paragraph. */
  .support {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-left: 48px;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    /* Stacked, the rule belongs above the support text rather than beside it. */
    .support {
      border-left: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      padding-left: 0;
      padding-top: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
